<!--CLI Documentation — Commands
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.cli.documentation.Commands-->
<clidoc:Commands xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:clidoc="com.machineblocks.bml.cli.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    User-facing commands for rendering BML to SCAD
  </is>
  <documentation><![CDATA[
    The host exposes a short command set. validate matches blockml validate.
    compile takes a BlockML type selector, not a file path and not --out.

    machineblocks validate [file]
    - Same project validate as blockml validate.
    - Exit 0 success, 1 diagnostics, 2 config or usage.
    - Does not register the SCAD target and does not write SCAD.
    - A file argument validates that file. --all validates the reachable corpus.
      file and --all together exit 2.

    machineblocks compile <source-selector>
    - Compiles with target machineblocks-v3-scad.
    - The selector is one BlockML type selector: an exact block FQN, a package
      selector ending in .*, or a recursive selector ending in .**.
      Resolution is scanTypes from the BlockML framework. This host does not
      define a second selector language.
    - --source-package <FQN> is the source package root for an explicit mapping.
    - --target-package <FQN> is the target package root. It is not a directory
      and not the FQN of one output file.
    - --help shows this command.
    - There is no --out and no --all. The output root is the configured srcDir
      (default blocks).
    - A selector only chooses blocks. It does not by itself choose the target
      package, except that a package selector (a final .* or .** segment)
      supplies the source root when --target-package is set and
      --source-package is omitted. An exact block FQN does not supply a source
      root.
    - --source-package without --target-package exits 2 with
      MB_SOURCE_PACKAGE_ALONE.
    - --target-package without a derivable source root exits 2 with
      MB_SOURCE_PACKAGE_REQUIRED.
    - A missing selector, an unknown flag, or a selector scanTypes rejects
      exits 2.
    - Types whose baseType chain is neither com.machineblocks.bml.core.Block
      nor com.machineblocks.bml.core.Set are skipped. If none remain, the host
      exits 1 with MB_SELECTOR_EMPTY and the selector text.
    - Mapping failures, collisions, and paths that leave srcDir or would
      overwrite a .bml file exit 1. No output file is written unless every
      selected block has a target FQN and a legal path, and every compile
      succeeded.
    - Exit 0 writes the SCAD or preset JSON files and a sibling .map when the
      target attached a source map.

    Host diagnostic codes:

    - MB_SOURCE_PACKAGE_ALONE — --source-package without --target-package.
    - MB_SOURCE_PACKAGE_REQUIRED — --target-package and the source root is not
      determined. The message names --source-package.
    - MB_SELECTOR_EMPTY — the selector matched no Block or Set.
    - MB_TARGET_COLLISION — two selected blocks share a target FQN or output path.
    - MB_OUTPUT_ESCAPES_SRC — a resolved path is outside srcDir.
    - MB_OUTPUT_OVERWRITES_BML — a resolved path is an existing .bml file.

    Mapping codes MB_TARGET_PACKAGE_UNDETERMINED, MB_TARGET_PACKAGE_AMBIGUOUS,
    and MB_SOURCE_OUTSIDE_ROOT are defined with the manifestation rules.

    machineblocks --help
    - Lists these commands.
    - Points advanced users to blockml --help for search, inspect, graph,
      transform, new, and init.

    Not in this host surface (still available via blockml if that package
    is installed): watch, search, inspect, graph, transform, scaffolding, xsd
    toggle, thumbnail generation.

    Per-target matrix entry this host satisfies:

        machineblocks-v3-scad — document target; selected by type selector;
        written under srcDir; registered by @machineblocks/cli, not by @blockml/cli.

  ]]></documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="clidoc:Configuration" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</clidoc:Commands>
